{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794527316324,"sessionID":"ses_e2dd83e38ffeLH4Ot77Rgtkbk7","part":{"partID":"prt_1d229c852001ZqTUGZi453vqJ5","sessionID":"ses_e2dd83e38ffeLH4Ot77Rgtkbk7","messageID":"msg_1d229bc2c001s2Glhy03d5NMXs","type":"tool","id":"call_a422b92905e349718b795647","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"spawn(\\|detached\\|daemon\" .skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs | head -50"},"output":"5:// ║ PURPOSE: Prepares advisor state and launches the resident daemon child.  ║\n39:// Load project-local env overrides BEFORE spawning the daemon child. .env.local wins over\n124:// A new owner has no socket until its daemon finishes starting. A second launcher\n149:  // advisor daemon child, so the advisor can never see it to attach a compiled\n154:  // Trusted roots for private `local-*` skill links. The daemon resolves each\n168:  // the scorer's env reader never sees them under normal daemon supervision\n219:        return path.join(socketDir, 'daemon-ipc.sock');\n561:async function reapOwnerBeforeRespawn(ownerPid, expectedExecutablePath = null) {\n583:  log(`reaping recorded skill-advisor daemon pid ${ownerPid} before respawn`);\n591:    log(`skill-advisor daemon pid ${ownerPid} exceeded ${RESPAWN_REAP_GRACE_MS}ms reap grace; sending SIGKILL`);\n609:// The CLI starts launchers detached, so a parent pid of 1 is the normal state\n826:// A daemon loads its code once at launch, so a build that lands afterwards leaves\n828:// Only a launched daemon counts: its lease carries a childPid and a startedAt\n843:// The stale-build recycle runs ahead of a bridge to a live daemon, so it passes\n855:    log('confirmed-dead socket but no recorded skill-advisor daemon pid is available; respawn inert');\n856:    writeLeaseHeldDiagnostic(leaseResult, ' (dead-socket-no-daemon-pid)');\n857:    return { action: 'report', reason: 'missing-daemon-pid', socketPath: decision.socketPath };\n875:    const reapResult = await reapOwnerBeforeRespawn(targetPid, expectedExecutablePath);\n877:      log(`dead-socket respawn skipped; ${reapResult.reason} for daemonPid=${targetPid}`);\n939:// still inside its startup grace, so a second client bridges to a daemon that is\n963:    log(`skill-advisor daemon for owner pid ${leaseResult.ownerPid} was launched before the current build; recycling it`);\n970:    log(`stale-build recycle skipped (${recycled.reason}); bridging to the running daemon`);\n1037:    const daemonLeasePath = path.join(runtimeDir, 'dist', 'runtime', 'lib', 'daemon', 'lease.js');\n1038:    const leaseModule = require(daemonLeasePath);\n1051:      log(`daemon lease check failed: ${error.message}`);\n1149:// because this launcher, the model server it spawns and the daemon child's\n1150:// embedding client all honour it, and the daemon socket keeps its own scoping.\n1444:    actions.push('built the @spec-kit/system-skill-advisor daemon against the installed dependencies');\n1446:    actions.push('installed dependencies and built the @spec-kit/system-skill-advisor daemon');\n1550:  childProcess = spawn(process.execPath, [server], {\n1651:        const reapResult = await reapOwnerBeforeRespawn(pendingBootstrapReapPid, reapExecutablePath);\n1653:          log(`stale launcher lease reap skipped; ${reapResult.reason} for daemonPid=${pendingBootstrapReapPid}`);\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"5:// ║ PURPOSE: Prepares advisor state and launches the resident daemon child.  ║\n39:// Load project-local env overrides BEFORE spawning the daemon child. .env.local wins over\n124:// A new owner has no socket until its daemon finishes starting. A second launcher\n149:  // advisor daemon child, so the advisor can never see it to attach a compiled\n154:  // Trusted roots for private `local-*` skill links. The daemon resolves each\n168:  // the scorer's env reader never sees them under normal daemon supervision\n219:       