{"type":"text","timestamp":1794527888322,"sessionID":"ses_e2dd83e38ffeLH4Ot77Rgtkbk7","part":{"id":"prt_1d2326f11002VJq11VXAQOwQWo","sessionID":"ses_e2dd83e38ffeLH4Ot77Rgtkbk7","messageID":"msg_1d23243c6001IkKyzCzIKELwan","type":"text","text":"T003 is complete and its literal checks pass, but the `0 of 5` result came from the warm daemon, not a cold start. Do not drop T024 to T026 on this number without a decision from you.\n\n**Files written**\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/scratch/cold-start.mjs`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/scratch/cold-start-before.txt`\n\n**Recorded run output**\n```\nrun 1: 468 ms | Advisor: stale; use sk-doc 0.95/0.15 pass.\nrun 2: 431 ms | Advisor: stale; use sk-doc 0.95/0.15 pass.\nrun 3: 424 ms | Advisor: stale; use sk-doc 0.95/0.15 pass.\nrun 4: 431 ms | Advisor: stale; use sk-doc 0.95/0.15 pass.\nrun 5: 585 ms | Advisor: stale; use sk-doc 0.95/0.15 pass.\nfail-open 0 of 5\n```\n\n**Verify results**\n- `wc -l` on the file prints `6`.\n- The last line matches `^fail-open [0-5] of 5$` (`MATCH`).\n- `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cold-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing, exit 1.\n- `ls /tmp/system-skill-advisor | wc -l` prints 39 before and 39 after the run.\n\n**Why the zero is not a cold-start measurement.** The checkout's daemon, pid 98950, was started at 00:53:09 and the recorded run finished at 00:53:47. With a live daemon, the launcher takes its `liveOwnerDetected` path and bridges to the lease holder instead of starting a daemon in the temporary socket directory. A probe with the same method showed five processes naming the temporary directory and no socket file created there, and no process survived the run. The 424 to 585 ms range is therefore a warm-daemon round trip. Median is 431 ms.\n\nOne environmental detail matters. At 00:50 the advisor dist was stale and the hook failed open with `dist is stale`, exit 69. Another worker rebuilt it at 00:52:59, so the recorded run used a fresh build. The earlier failure was not the measurement.\n\n**What I could not do.** I did not edit `tasks.md`, per the dispatch rule. The conditional text would be `Dropped: T003 measured fail-open 0 of 5` with median 431 ms on T024, T025 and T026. The measurement is warm-path, so I recommend a re-run with no live daemon for this checkout before applying it.\n\nWork state: both files are new and untracked. Nothing was committed or pushed.\n\nYour decision: either authorize stopping this checkout's advisor daemon and re-running `node $SP/cold-start.mjs --runs 5`, or accept this as warm-path evidence and leave T024 to T026 pending.","time":{"start":1794527883025,"end":1794527888322}}}
